s1-p3 = prose (cons "The consequence concerns what a description must retain. An action depends on the information available to its participant; an interpretation depends on the context in which an expression is received; a conclusion depends on the relations and evidence establishing it. These dependencies determine what a description establishes about the activity, not merely how it is written. The constructions developed here make those dependencies explicit and available to further activity, including activity that changes the descriptions and interpretations themselves. This is the subject of *hyperactivity*: routines, relations, and rationales acting on one another, rather than code acted upon by an unexplained intelligence outside the account." nil)
